# Trained model artifacts.
#
# These three ARE tracked. They are the project's deliverables: the team needs
# to share them, and a blanket "*.joblib" rule here is what silently swallowed
# an earlier "exported as joblib file" commit -- git accepted the commit and
# dropped the model, so the push looked successful and contained nothing.
# Together they are ~7 MB, which is fine for a normal git object.
#
#   artifacts/expense_category_model.joblib     transaction categorizer
#   artifacts/expense_forecaster_model.joblib   daily spend forecaster
#   artifacts/anomaly_model.joblib              + anomaly_category_stats.json
#
# Everything else in artifacts/ is scratch output from a training run and
# stays ignored, including the pre-2024 scikit-learn 0.24 pickles that no
# longer load on 1.x (recoverable from history at 77c2fd1 if ever needed).
artifacts/*
!artifacts/.gitignore
!artifacts/expense_category_model.joblib
!artifacts/expense_forecaster_model.joblib
!artifacts/anomaly_model.joblib
!artifacts/anomaly_category_stats.json
